---
title: "collect_profits (Sui Move Concepts: Capability-Gated Withdrawal)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_cap: verify ShopOwnerCap reference provided
    q_check_cap --> q_get_amount: cap is valid (ownership proven by reference)
    q_get_amount --> q_split: amount = shop.balance.value()
    q_split --> q_to_coin: profits = shop.balance.split(amount)
    q_to_coin --> q_transfer: coin = profits.into_coin(ctx)
    q_transfer --> [*]: transfer::public_transfer(coin, ctx.sender())

    note right of q_check_cap
        INV-001: ShopOwnerCap is passed by immutable reference (not consumed)
        INV-002: Only the cap holder can call collect_profits
        INV-003: Cap ownership is enforced by Sui runtime (address-owned object auth)
    end note

    note right of q_split
        INV-004: Entire shop balance is withdrawn (amount = balance.value())
        INV-005: After split, shop.balance becomes zero
    end note

    note right of q_transfer
        INV-006: Profits go to transaction sender (cap owner)
        INV-007: Coin has public_transfer because Coin has store ability
    end note
